# =============================================================================
# config.local.example — template for ~/.ssh/config.local
# =============================================================================
# config.local is the per-machine, UNTRACKED SSH config. The main ~/.ssh/config
# includes it BEFORE the dotshell-tracked config.homelab, so anything here
# OVERRIDES the shared config (ssh is first-match-wins).
#
# To use: copy this to ~/.ssh/config.local and uncomment what you need.
#   cp ~/.ssh/config.local.example ~/.ssh/config.local
# Everything below is commented out, so a fresh copy is inert until you edit it.
#
# Rule of thumb:
#   - Want it on EVERY workstation?  -> put it in config.homelab and commit it.
#   - Just here / secret / a local override?  -> put it here.
#   - Recreating the same block on multiple machines?  -> promote it to config.homelab.
# =============================================================================


# --- Hosts reachable only from THIS machine ---------------------------------
# A work bastion, client server, or VM that only exists on this box's network/VPN.
# No reason to sync these to every workstation.
#
# Host work-bastion
#   HostName bastion.example-corp.com
#   User azmievski
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_work
#
# Host clientbox
#   HostName 10.50.0.12
#   User deploy
#   ProxyJump work-bastion


# --- Private hosts / IPs / usernames you don't want committed ----------------
# Even in your own repo, keep client/third-party identifiers off the shared,
# syncing file.
#
# Host personal-vps
#   HostName <ip-or-host>
#   User <user>
#   Port 2222


# --- Per-machine override of a SHARED host ----------------------------------
# Wins over config.homelab because this file is included first. Examples:
#
# Reach oslo through a jump host from this machine only (e.g. when off-LAN),
# while other machines go direct:
# Host oslo
#   ProxyJump somejump
#
# Force agent forwarding off on a less-trusted machine:
# Host minion
#   ForwardAgent no
#
# Temporarily pin a shared host to a different key/agent during a migration:
# Host sofia
#   IdentityAgent ~/.ssh/some-other-agent.sock
#   IdentitiesOnly yes


# --- Machine-specific key / agent paths -------------------------------------
# If a key or the 1Password socket lives somewhere nonstandard on this machine,
# override it here instead of branching the shared file.
#
# Host *
#   IdentityAgent "~/Library/Group Containers/2BUA8C4S2C.com.1password/t/agent.sock"


# --- Local tunnels / forwards set up on this machine ------------------------
# Host dbtunnel
#   HostName oslo
#   LocalForward 5432 127.0.0.1:5432


# --- Temporary / experimental blocks ----------------------------------------
# Try a new host or option here first; once proven, promote it to config.homelab
# and commit. (The oslo 1Password-agent setup started life as a scoped trial.)
